{
 "corpus": "galileo",
 "seat": "EA-CORPORA-30/05",
 "title": "Galileo: Sidereus nuncius (1610), Il Saggiatore (1623), the Dialogo (1632), the Discorsi (1638) and the Lettera a Cristina di Lorena (1615, printed 1636)",
 "edition": "Galileo Galilei, Sidereus nuncius (Venetiis: apud Thomam Baglionum, 1610), the first printing, Smithsonian Libraries (Dibner) copy, scan and OCR layer; Galileo Galilei, Sidereus nuncius, in Favaro, Le opere di Galileo Galilei, vol. III.1 (1892), Latin Wikisource, with Favaro's variants from the manuscript draft; Galileo Galilei, Il Saggiatore, nel quale con bilancia esquisita e giusta si ponderano le cose contenute nella Libra astronomica e filosofica di Lotario Sarsi Sigensano (Roma: Giacomo Mascardi, 1623), the first printing, University of Toronto copy, scan and OCR layer; Galileo Galilei, Il Saggiatore, in Favaro, Le opere di Galileo Galilei, vol. VI (1896), Italian Wikisource: the dedication to Urban VIII, the preface and the fifty-three sections; Galileo Galilei, Dialogo … sopra i due massimi sistemi del mondo tolemaico, e copernicano (Fiorenza: per Gio. Batista Landini, 1632), the first printing, Smithsonian Libraries copy, scan and OCR layer; Galileo Galilei, Dialogo sopra i due massimi sistemi del mondo tolemaico e copernicano, in Favaro, Le opere di Galileo Galilei, vol. VII (1897), Italian Wikisource: the dedication, Al discreto lettore and the four days; Galileo Galilei, Discorsi e dimostrazioni matematiche, intorno à due nuove scienze attenenti alla mecanica & i movimenti locali (Leida: appresso gli Elsevirii, 1638), the first printing, University of Toronto (Stillman Drake) copy, scan and OCR layer; Galileo Galilei, Discorsi e dimostrazioni matematiche intorno a due nuove scienze, in Favaro, Le opere di Galileo Galilei, vol. VIII (1898), Italian Wikisource: the dedication to the Conte di Noailles, the printer's note and the four days (the Appendix on centres of gravity is not transcribed there); Galileo Galilei, Nov-antiqua sanctissimorum patrum, & probatorum theologorum doctrina de Sacrae Scripturae testimoniis, in conclusionibus mere naturalibus … temere non usurpandis (Augustae Treboc.: impensis Elzeviriorum, typis Davidis Hautti, 1636), the Lettera a Madama Cristina di Lorena (1615) in its first printing, Italian with Elia Diodati's Latin version, University of Toronto copy, scan and OCR layer; Galileo Galilei, Lettera a Madama Cristina di Lorena, Granduchessa di Toscana (1615), in Favaro, Le opere di Galileo Galilei, vol. V (1895), Italian Wikisource",
 "language": "mul",
 "license": {
  "payload": "Per item, recorded in origin.items. Galileo Galilei died in 1642; the printings of 1610, 1623, 1632, 1636 and 1638 are in the public domain everywhere. The Internet Archive copies carry these statements: Sidereus nuncius (Smithsonian Libraries) 'Not in copyright'; Il Saggiatore, the Discorsi and the Nov-antiqua (University of Toronto, Fisher Library), and the Dialogo (Smithsonian Libraries), no rights statement. The transcriptions are from Antonio Favaro's Edizione Nazionale, Le opere di Galileo Galilei (Firenze: Barbèra, 1890–1909), volumes III, V, VI, VII and VIII (1892–1898), public domain in the United States (published before 1931) and Favaro's own term run (died 1922); the Wikisource pages are CC BY-SA 4.0 for the site's contributions, redistributed under the same licence.",
  "record": "CC-BY-4.0 applies to this seat record only."
 },
